in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @nl
in @mirror/store
in @mirror/au
in @mirror/mosaic
in @code

# @mirror/store/crystal — the polyglot, content-addressed, self-executable
# artifact the kintsugi build settles into; altitude-4 of the build lifecycle.
#
# THE 2026-06-16 RECOGNITION (Alex + Reed → Mara). The kintsugi build
# lifecycle has four altitudes; the substrate already named three; this
# shard names the fourth:
#
#   1. spec     — `mirror.spec`, parsed into `manifold`. Inert declaration.
#                  Lives at `@mirror/spec` (shards/mirror/spec.mirror).
#   2. settle   — the kintsugi loop running; `@kintsugi/oscillate` drives
#                  it; the ACTIVE/DARK alternation per recognition #51.
#   3. verdict  — the property-chain record; `[property_verdict]` from
#                  @glass; Narrative-shape wire form per `@mirror/spectral`.
#   4. crystal  — THE OUTPUT. Polyglot. Content-addressed. Self-executable.
#                  What this shard declares.
#
# stage_play (Gleam library at /Users/reed/dev/projects/stage_play/) is the
# proximate inspiration. Its `Story → Play → Narrative` triad surfaces the
# form/process/record partition cleanly (recognition #55: form-side names
# state observation; process-side names transformation; record-side names
# the verdict trace). stage_play HAS no altitude-4 — dataflow pipelines
# don't produce artifacts; they produce reductions. Mirror has altitude-4
# because mirror's settle PRODUCES something downstream consumers run.
# That something IS the crystal.
#
# === Polyglot by construction ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING STRUCTURAL CLAIM. The crystal cannot be non-polyglot
# because the spec doesn't compile to one language. Every kintsugi settle
# emits at multiple @code/<lang> altitudes simultaneously: a target may
# settle to @code/rust as a binary AND emit @ci/github YAML alongside AND
# project @code/typescript bindings for a runtime peer. The `crystal`
# carrier preserves those altitude boundaries STRUCTURALLY — no
# language-erasure happens at the artifact altitude.
#
# `composition_graph: mosaic(@code)` IS the structural enforcement. mosaic
# (shards/mirror/mosaic.mirror) declares `type mosaic(altitude) = ref` as
# the universal parametric composition carrier; the @code-altitude
# specialization names a DAG whose nodes are `@code/<lang>` grammars and
# whose edges are compilation dependencies. The substrate rejects a
# crystal whose composition_graph is malformed (cycles, dangling references,
# missing @code/* nodes) because the @code-altitude mosaic algebra is
# closed under well-typed composition.
#
# === Deployment is shift, not a separate noun ===
#
# The substrate does NOT need a `deployment` type. `shift(crystal) ->
# @io/runtime` IS the deployment — one of the five operations applied at
# the crystal altitude. Per shards/mirror/mosaic.mirror line 140: `shift
# is where @io crossings happen`. The crystal's glass block below carries
# all five operations; shift is the one that relocates the crystal to a
# runtime.
#
# === The five fields ===
#
# Per the recognition; each field grounded in existing substrate vocabulary
# (the substrate-already-had-the-word pattern, instance ~63):
#
#   oid: oid
#     The content-address of the settled artifact. Per @mirror/store/oid
#     (the sibling sub-prism at shards/mirror/store.mirror lines 82-105):
#     `type oid = ref`. The crystal's identity IS its oid; two crystals
#     with byte-equal field tuples have the same oid and ARE the same
#     crystal. This is the inherited identity contract from @glass's
#     splinter / shard floor.
#
#   section: [splinter(@code)]
#     Language-section structure. Each splinter lives at an `@code/<lang>`
#     altitude (per @glass's `type splinter(altitude)` — the universal
#     content-addressed atom parametric over altitude). The list preserves
#     ordering AND altitude boundaries: section[0] may be @code/rust at
#     OID(A); section[1] may be @code/typescript at OID(B); the same
#     crystal carries both without language-erasure. Substrate-pull
#     correct: the substrate already has `splinter(altitude)` (glass.mirror)
#     and `splinter(ast)` (the parametric quote primitive #54); `[splinter
#     (@code)]` specializes the carrier to the language-section altitude.
#
#   derived_predicates: [property_verdict]
#     The properties the kintsugi loop verified during settlement. Per
#     @glass's `type property_verdict = { verdict: verdict, where: location
#     }` — a verdict located at a glass-wall site. Each derived predicate
#     is a (property, verdict, location) triple the loop ran during the
#     settle pass. Substrate-pull-correct: this is BYTE-IDENTICAL to
#     @mirror/shatter's section-3 `properties: [property_verdict]` field
#     (shards/mirror/shatter.mirror line ~120). The shatter was the
#     altitude-1 (au) projection; the crystal is the altitude-4 (artifact)
#     projection; same carrier, same verdicts, different lifecycle phase.
#
#   fracture_calendar: transparency(au)
#     au<T>'s gold-cracks made structural. The loss carrier from @glass
#     (transparency(p) = success | partial(opacity_map) | failure(opacity_map)).
#     Each opacity is a located fact carrying property + weight (per
#     glass.mirror line 117); the opacity_map IS the calendar — the
#     timeline of fractures scheduled for future kintsugi passes. The
#     substrate-pull recognition: au's `transparency` field (au.mirror
#     line 145) carries the residual loss at the proposal phase; the
#     crystal's `fracture_calendar` carries the SAME residual at the
#     artifact phase. The loop chose not to close these cracks; the
#     calendar names what's still open. Cybersyn's algedonic loop names
#     the same shape at the substance altitude: pain signals scheduled
#     for next-cycle attention; here the signals are typed transparency
#     opacities. Recognition #53 (property/fracture bilateral pattern):
#     fracture_calendar is the substrate's altitude-4 instance of the
#     pattern — the property side declared the gates; the fracture side
#     wrote the morphisms; the crystal carries the cracks the morphisms
#     didn't close.
#
#   composition_graph: mosaic(@code)
#     The DAG over @code/<lang> grammars. Per @mirror/mosaic's `type
#     mosaic(altitude) = ref` (the universal parametric composition
#     carrier, mosaic.mirror lines 60-94): mosaic IS the composition form
#     at every altitude; the @code-altitude specialization carries the
#     polyglot DAG. Each node references an `@code/<lang>` grammar; each
#     edge is a compilation dependency. The substrate enforces well-
#     formedness through the @code-altitude mosaic algebra (no cycles,
#     no dangling refs, no missing @code/* nodes). This IS the polyglot-
#     by-construction structural witness.
#
# === The four sub-type choices: substrate-pull reading ===
#
# Every non-oid field rides an existing substrate carrier:
#
#   section            ← splinter(altitude) at @glass (glass.mirror)
#                         specialized via `splinter(@code)` — the same
#                         parametric-quote primitive #54 used.
#   derived_predicates ← property_verdict at @glass (glass.mirror line ~154)
#                         — identical shape to shatter's section-3.
#   fracture_calendar  ← transparency(au) at @glass (glass.mirror line ~137)
#                         — au's loss carrier lifted to artifact altitude;
#                         identical shape to shatter's section-2.
#   composition_graph  ← mosaic(@code) at @mirror/mosaic (mosaic.mirror)
#                         — the parametric universal carrier specialized
#                         to the @code namespace altitude.
#
# No new types invented at this shard. Four existing carriers, composed.
# The crystal IS what falls out of altitude-4 when the substrate's prior
# vocabulary is read at the artifact altitude. Substrate-already-had-the-
# word; this shard names what was already in scope.
#
# === Relationship to neighboring altitudes ===
#
# crystal vs au (shards/mirror/au.mirror): au is the SINGLE-ALTITUDE
# Fate-emitted proposal at the settle altitude; crystal is the MULTI-
# ALTITUDE settled artifact at the post-settle altitude. au carries one
# `altitude: ref` field (the target altitude of the proposal); crystal
# carries a `composition_graph: mosaic(@code)` field (the DAG of all
# altitudes the artifact composes). au is what Fate emits; crystal is
# what kintsugi crystallizes from the settled au through the property
# chain. settle is the Kleisli arrow `au -> Imperfect<shard>`; the
# shard's stored composition at the multi-altitude artifact phase IS
# the crystal.
#
# crystal vs shard (shards/glass.mirror): shard is the uuid_spectral-
# addressed settled MIDDLE-layer composition (the bottom-top-middle
# recognition's middle); crystal is what one or more shards compose
# into at the polyglot-artifact altitude. A shard carries
# `splinters: [splinter(altitude)]` at one altitude per shard; a
# crystal's `section: [splinter(@code)]` carries the artifact's
# language sections across the @code altitudes. The shard is the
# storage primitive; the crystal is the deployable artifact.
#
# crystal vs shatter (shards/mirror/shatter.mirror): shatter is the
# .shatter file disk projection — a single-altitude AST projection
# with five sections. The crystal carries shatter's section-2
# (transparency) AND section-3 (properties) IDENTICALLY, plus
# language-section structure (`section`), plus the polyglot DAG
# (`composition_graph`). shatter and crystal are sibling projections
# at different lifecycle phases — shatter is altitude-1 (the au
# proposal made disk-portable); crystal is altitude-4 (the settled
# multi-altitude artifact). The shatter pair (`project`/`ingest`)
# round-trips; the crystal's settled form is what `shift(crystal)
# -> @io/runtime` relocates.
#
# crystal vs manifold (shards/mirror/spec.mirror): manifold is the
# altitude-1 declaration shape (`mirror.spec` parsed); crystal is
# the altitude-4 output shape. The four altitudes lift one to the
# next: manifold → settle → verdict → crystal. Each altitude reads
# the prior; each emits to the next. The crystal is what the
# substrate hands to the runtime when the loop closes.
#
# === Why `glass` and not `prism` at this sub-prism path ===
#
# Per shards/mirror/store.mirror's `@mirror/store/oid` precedent
# (lines 94-100): sub-prism declarations under a parent prism use
# `glass`, not `prism`. The path-namespace property
# (@epistemologic/property/path_matches_namespace) verifies that
# `shards/mirror/store/crystal.mirror` declares ONLY the namespace
# `@mirror/store/crystal` at sub-prism form.
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per [[feedback-substrate-pull]]: every type below rides a carrier
# the substrate already declared. Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]:
# every field is a typed newtype or parametric carrier; no bare `f64`,
# `string`, or `[T]` escapes. Per [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-
# everything]]: the five-operation glass block IS the canonical
# declaration form. Per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]:
# the four sub-type choices honour the prior vocabulary; no invention.
#
# === Forward-promised actions ===
#
# The crystal's life-cycle actions land downstream when consumers
# pull. Sketched, not declared this tick (per [[feedback-craft-not-
# deliver]]):
#
#   crystallize(s: shard, m: mosaic(@code)) -> imperfect(crystal)
#     The constructor. Compose a settled shard's splinters with the
#     project's composition_graph; verify the @code-altitude mosaic
#     algebra closes; emit imperfect<crystal> with transparency
#     carrying the residual cracks (the fracture_calendar's source).
#
#   verify_composition(c: crystal) -> verdict
#     The polyglot-by-construction integrity check. Walks the
#     composition_graph; verifies every `@code/<lang>` node resolves;
#     verifies no cycles; verifies every edge's compilation
#     dependency holds. Returns @glass.verdict.
#
#   shift @io/runtime(c: crystal) -> runtime_handle
#     The deployment. `shift` at the crystal altitude relocates the
#     artifact to @io/runtime. The substrate-pull-correct form: not a
#     separate `deploy` action; the five-operation algebra ALREADY
#     carries the relocation verb. Lands when @io/runtime is named.
#
# These actions stay forward-promised this tick. The substrate-decl is
# the carrier; the actions are the next consumers' pull.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
# Each face of the crystal recognition has prior art; no system
# composes them all:
#
#   content-addressed artifact   Nix (Dolstra 2003); Bazel (Google
#                                 2010); IPFS (Benet 2014). Same
#                                 content → same hash → same artifact;
#                                 the substrate's altitude-4 instance
#                                 of the substrate-already-had-the-
#                                 word build-system recognition.
#   polyglot composition         WebAssembly Component Model (W3C
#                                 2023); GraalVM (Oracle 2018). The
#                                 substrate's composition_graph IS
#                                 the @code-altitude mosaic; the
#                                 polyglot boundary is structural,
#                                 not coordinated through a runtime
#                                 host.
#   self-executable              Java JAR (Sun 1996); Erlang escript
#                                 (~1998); Docker image (2013). The
#                                 substrate's `shift(crystal) ->
#                                 @io/runtime` IS the same verb
#                                 across the prior art.
#   crystal noun                 Smalltalk image (Xerox PARC 1980);
#                                 LISP core (1960+); the metaphor of
#                                 a settled-running-system snapshot.
#                                 The substrate's crystal is what
#                                 that snapshot IS at altitude-4.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/mirror-store.md (the @mirror/store family
#               that crystal extends);
#               docs/specs/mosaic.md §7 (the .shatter / crystal
#               sibling projection altitude);
#               docs/specs/au-and-conductivity.md (au's transparency
#               carrier; crystal's fracture_calendar lifts the same).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]
#                      (#55; crystal IS the record-side artifact),
#                      [[architecture-fragmentation-is-the-rust-substrate]]
#                      (the @mirror/store altitude crystal extends).
# Memory: [[architecture-splinter-and-spectral-db-edges]],
#         [[architecture-mirror-as-content-addressed-build-system]] (#43;
#         crystal IS the build-system's output altitude),
#         [[reference-mirror-spectral-spec]] (the kintsugi-as-oscillation
#         spec; the loop the crystal falls out of).
# Related shards: store.mirror (the parent prism; @mirror/store/oid is
#                 the sibling sub-prism; crystal's oid field rides it),
#                 glass.mirror (splinter / property_verdict / transparency
#                 carriers — crystal's three non-oid non-graph fields),
#                 mosaic.mirror (mosaic(altitude) — crystal's composition_graph),
#                 au.mirror (the proposal phase crystal is the artifact
#                 phase of), spec.mirror (the manifold crystal is the
#                 settlement-output of), shatter.mirror (the sibling
#                 projection at the .shatter altitude).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/mirror/store/crystal.mirror`
# declares `@mirror/store/crystal` (and only that).

# === The crystal sub-prism ===
#
# Per shards/mirror/store.mirror's @mirror/store/oid precedent: a
# sub-prism declared under the parent @mirror/store. The five-operation
# block carries crystal's algebra at the artifact altitude:
#
#   focus crystal    observe a crystal's state (oid + sections + verdicts).
#   project crystal  filter a crystal by what matters (specific
#                     @code/<lang> section; specific predicate verdict).
#   split crystal    explore the composition_graph's structure;
#                     enumerate the DAG's nodes and edges.
#   shift crystal    the deployment verb. Relocates the crystal to
#                     @io/runtime. NOT a separate noun; the substrate's
#                     five-operation algebra ALREADY carries this.
#   settle crystal   crystallize a settled shard into a crystal (the
#                     constructor; verifies the composition algebra
#                     closes; the kintsugi loop's altitude-4 output).
glass @mirror/store/crystal {
  focus crystal
  project crystal
  split crystal
  shift crystal
  settle crystal
}

# === the crystal record ===
#
# Five fields. Four substrate-pull carriers + the oid identity.
#
# Identity contract (inherited from @glass's content-addressing floor):
# a crystal's identity IS its oid, computed from byte-equal
# (section, derived_predicates, fracture_calendar, composition_graph)
# under the substrate's content-address algebra (CoincidenceHash<5,5>
# per shards/prism.mirror's spectral-triple framing). Two crystals
# with equal field tuples have the same oid and ARE the same
# crystal. This is the substrate-altitude statement of polyglot-by-
# construction's reproducibility: same settlement, same crystal,
# byte-equal — regardless of how many @code/<lang> altitudes the
# composition spans.
#
# After settle:
#
#   shard's splinters → composed → composition_graph verified →
#   property chain run → derived_predicates accumulated →
#   residual transparency → fracture_calendar → crystal emitted.
#
# After shift:
#
#   shift crystal -> @io/runtime → the artifact runs.
type crystal = {
  # The content-address of the settled artifact. Per @mirror/store/oid.
  oid: oid,

  # Language-section structure. Each splinter at its own @code/<lang>
  # altitude; the list preserves altitude boundaries within the
  # content-addressed atom. Per @glass's splinter(altitude) carrier
  # specialized to the @code namespace.
  section: [splinter(@code)],

  # Properties the kintsugi loop verified during settlement. Same
  # carrier as shatter's section-3 (shards/mirror/shatter.mirror).
  # Per @glass's property_verdict = { verdict, where: location }.
  derived_predicates: [property_verdict],

  # au<T>'s gold-cracks made structural — the timeline of opacities
  # the loop chose not to close, scheduled for future kintsugi
  # passes. Same carrier as shatter's section-2; the loss field of
  # au lifted to artifact altitude. Per @glass's transparency(p).
  fracture_calendar: transparency(au),

  # The DAG over @code/<lang> grammars — the polyglot-by-construction
  # structural witness. Per @mirror/mosaic's mosaic(altitude)
  # specialized to the @code namespace. The substrate rejects a
  # malformed composition_graph at this altitude.
  composition_graph: mosaic(@code),
}

out @mirror/store/crystal
out crystal
